  "title": "More apps, easier to find",
  "summary": "The app garden grew, while new models, a media API, and clearer documentation made more of Pollinations useful to build with.\n\nThe community showcase grew across creative tools, learning apps, bots, developer utilities, and illustrated storytelling. Eighteen missing apps were restored, while purpose and genre filters plus platform badges made the catalog easier to browse. By February 26, all 562 listed apps had platform labels. A roundup of six submissions consolidated showcase entries rather than adding six more distinct apps.\n\nAlpha models `nomnom` and `polly` added research and tool-assisted workflows. The paid `claude` route moved to Sonnet 4.6; `gemini-large` moved to Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview; and `minimax` moved to M2.5. Image generation gained alpha `grok-imagine` and paid `seedream5` and `nanobanana-2`. Existing Gemini 3 Pro names kept their original target rather than changing under callers.\n\nA new API accepts file, raw-binary, or base64 uploads and returns a public URL. Later in the week it gained support for arbitrary binary files and authenticated deletion by the uploader; the final upload limit is 10 MB. A separate `/video/{prompt}` route, custom ElevenLabs voice IDs, and fixes to video model routing and reference images broadened the ways to work with media.\n\nThe API reference was reorganized by task, with cURL, Python, JavaScript, browser-URL examples, and compact docs for AI agents. Model listings gained `context_length` for 21 text models, replacing the old `context_window` field for clients that read it. Updated submission guidelines, Hello and Community pages, and setup packages also made it easier to find a way into the project.",
